<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Koźle</h1><p class="st-meta">1303 CE – 1355 CE (approx.) · capital Koźle</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A minor Upper Silesian Piast duchy around the Oder town of Koźle, carved from the lands of the dukes of Bytom in the early 14th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kozle">Koźle</a> belonged to the Upper Silesian lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bytom">Duchy of Bytom</a>, ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Silesian Piasts</a>. Around 1303 it was set apart for a junior member of the dynasty, beginning a short history as a separate duchy, though for much of the period it was held together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bytom">Bytom</a> itself.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other small Silesian duchies, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kozle">Koźle</a> was a fortified market town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a> with surrounding villages, settled partly by German colonists under German town law. In 1327 its duke did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia">King John of Bohemia</a>, making the duchy a fief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a>. Little else is recorded of its government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Bytom-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kozle">Koźle</a> line ended in 1355, and after a dispute Koźle passed to the dukes of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-olesnica">Duchy of Oleśnica</a>, who held it until the late 15th century. It later reverted to the Bohemian crown, followed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1742 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1303 CE – 1355 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.63%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1303 CE – 1355 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Koźle</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Władysław of Bytom</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Cosel</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1329&amp;focus=duchy-of-kozle" aria-label="Duchy of Koźle on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5095 429 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Koźle lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5415 685L5432 684M5415 685L5330 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5432 684h0M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5415 685h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5415 685h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Koźle. <a href="/atlas?year=1329&amp;focus=duchy-of-kozle">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
